Void:
In java return type is mandatory if a method wont return anything then we have to declare the method with void return type. But in C language return type is optional and default return type is int.

Goto:
Usage of created several problems in old languages and hence sun people banned this keyword in java.

Const:
Use final instead of const.

Note: Goto and const are unused keywords and if we are trying to use to use then we will get compile time error.

                                               Reserved Literals:
 - True, false, null
 Here true and false are values for boolean data type
 Here null is default value for object reference

 Enum (1.5v)
 We can use enum to define a group of named constants

 Example:
 we can use enum to define a group of named constants
            enum month                         enum beer
